  "title": "The Time-Travel Garage",
  "hook": "Brian is SURE cars have always run on petrol — until a cardboard time machine takes the team on a trip through history.",
  "reading_minutes": 7,
  "core_lesson": "Cars haven't always used petrol — people tried steam, electric and petrol. Keep an open mind and check before you say 'always'.",
  "new_terms": [
    "history",
    "timeline"
  ],
  "adult_safety_note": "The time travel is a clearly marked imagination sequence inside a cardboard box. No real vehicles, fuel or batteries are used. Historical facts are simplified for age 7 and should be checked by a reviewer before release.",
  "localisation_key_prefix": "s01e05",
  "editorial_status": "draft",
  "learning_objectives": [
    {
      "topic": "History",
      "goal": "Before cars, people walked and used horses. Inventors tried steam-powered road vehicles over 250 years ago."
    },
    {
      "topic": "History",
      "goal": "More than 100 years ago, steam, electric and petrol cars all shared the roads."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Science",
      "goal": "Early electric cars were quiet and easy to start but couldn't go very far; petrol cars could go farther. Better batteries brought electric cars back."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Order",
      "goal": "Put kinds of transport on a timeline from long ago to today."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Open-mindedness",
      "goal": "Brian learns to check facts instead of saying 'always', and to welcome new ideas."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Safety",
      "goal": "Imagination play happens in a safe cardboard 'time machine' on the floor."
    }
  ],
  "talk_together": [
    "Brian said cars ALWAYS used petrol. What did he find out?",
    "Ask a grown-up: how did they travel when they were little? How is it different now?",
    "What do you think cars of the future will use? Why?"
  ],
